    {
      "version": "v1.8.22",
      "name": "v1.8.22",
      "published_at": "2026-09-08T04:30:50Z",
      "body": "Version 1.8.22 - Session keep-alive and auth robustness\n\nKeep the OpenSubtitles session alive while the app is open, and stop\ntransient network failures from logging users out.\n\nThe app stores a server-issued PHPSESSID as its session token. The server\nexpires it six hours after the last request (Set-Cookie Max-Age=21600),\nand nothing was refreshing it.\n\nSession keep-alive:\n- Add XmlRpcService.noOperation() and an hourly keep-alive ping\n- Ping is best-effort: it never mutates authentication state, because\n  NoOperation answers 200 OK even for tokens the server never issued\n- Guard against timer stacking, stale in-flight state, and hung sockets\n- Revalidate with a fresh GetUserInfo on wake/refocus after an idle gap,\n  bypassing the one-hour user-info cache\n\nAuthentication fixes:\n- checkAuthStatus no longer discards stored credentials when the server\n  is simply unreachable; only an actual rejection logs the user out\n- Return the verdict instead of stashing it on the service singleton,\n  which two concurrent StrictMode inits could clobber\n- Retry an unverified session when connectivity returns\n- Await restoreAuthFromStorage; a promise is always truthy\n\nLatent bugs found by fixing the ESLint parser:\n- updateService: downloadPath/totalBytes were block-scoped to the try but\n  read in the catch, so the signature-validation download fallback threw\n  ReferenceError instead of running\n- DebugPanel: same pattern left the older-browser clipboard fallback dead\n\nSecurity:\n- Stop logging partial session ids and tokens in SessionManager,\n  sessionUtils, DebugPanel and TryUploadSubtitles\n- DebugPanel no longer copies a token prefix into the clipboard blob\n- Escape the token in every XML-RPC request body\n\nHousekeeping:\n- ESLint ecmaVersion 2021 -> 2022; static class fields broke the parser,\n  leaving eight service files silently unlinted\n- Store the session under the key detectSession actually reads, and purge\n  the orphaned write-only opensubtitles_session_id\n- Collapse two XML escapers into one, and make it null-safe\n- Sync Cargo.lock, stale since 1.8.18",
